h1 Include Media mixin
.source_info
    p Using 
        a(href='http://include-media.com/') @include-media
    p
        a(href='http://include-media.com/documentation') Official documentation
        
section.source_section
    h2 Media mixin
    h3 Default usage
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media($breakpoint) {
        |   ...
        |}
    
    h3 With a single set breakpoint
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media('&gt;phone') {
        |   ...
        |}
    h3 With two set breakpoints
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media('&gt;phone', '&lt;=tablet') {
        |   ...
        |} 
    h3 With custom values
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media('&gt;=358px', '&lt;850px') {
        |   ...
        |} 
    h3 With set breakpoints with custom values
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media('&gt;desktop', '&lt;=1350px') {
        |   ...
        |} 

    h3 With a static expression
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media('retina2x') {
        |   ...
        |} 

    h3 Mixing everything
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media('&gt;=350px', '&lt;tablet', 'retina3x') {
        |   ...
        |}
        
section.source_section
    h2 Media-context mixin
    p Mixin allows redefining viariables just for the scope of the call.
    p It is helpful when having a component needing an extended configuration such as custom breakpoints (referred to as tweakpoints).
    
    h3 Default usage
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media-context($variables) {
        |   .foo {
        |      @include media($breakpoints) {
        |           ...
        |       }
        |   }
        |}

    h3 Extend the global breakpoints with a tweakpoint
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media-context(('custom': 678px)) {
        |   .foo {
        |       @include media('&gt;phone', '&lt;=custom') {
        |           ...
        |       }
        |   }
        |}

    h3 Extend the global media expressions with a custom one
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media-context($tweak-media-expressions: ('all': 'all')) {
        |   .foo {
        |       @include media('all', '&gt;phone') {
        |           ...
        |       }
        |   }
        |}

    h3 Extend both configuration maps
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |@include media-context(('custom': 678px), ('all': 'all')) {
        |   .foo {
        |       @include media('all', '&gt;phone', '&lt;=custom') {
        |           ...
        |       }
        |   }
        |}
        
section.source_section
    h2 Variables
    h3 Breakpoints
    p Breakpoints are stored in basic key:value map. They can be changed by user (see below)
    h4 Default values
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |$breakpoints: (
        |   'phone': 320px,
        |   'tablet': 768px,
        |   'desktop': 1024px
        |) !default;
    h4 Changing breakpoints
    em Creates a single breakpoint with the label phone (overrides the default value)
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |$breakpoints: ('phone': 456px);
        
    h3 Media Expressions
    p Media expressions and types are stored in basic key:value map. They can be changed by user (see below), although there is not much reason to do so
    h4 Default values
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |$media-expressions: (
        |   'screen': 'screen',
        |   'print': 'print',
        |   'handheld': 'handheld',
        |   'landscape': '(orientation: landscape)',
        |   'portrait': '(orientation: portrait)',
        |   'retina2x': '(-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 2), (min-resolution: 192dpi)',
        |   'retina3x': '(-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 3), (min-resolution: 350dpi)'
        |) !default;

    h4 Changing single media expression
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |$media-expressions: ('screen': 'screen');

    h4 Changing expression with logical OR operator
    code.src-js.source_visible
        |$media-expressions: (
        |   'retina2x': '(-webkit-min-device-pixel-ratio: 2), (min-resolution: 192dpi)'
        |);